        }
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Method",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Place the pork belly in a saucepan of cold water. Bring to the boil, then simmer for 25 to 30 minutes until cooked through. Remove and cool, then slice thinly.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Bring the same pan back to the boil. Add the prawns and cook for 2 to 3 minutes until pink and just cooked. Drain and halve lengthways.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Cook the rice noodles according to the packet. Drain, rinse with cold water, and leave to cool.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Make the dipping sauce. Mix the fish sauce, lime juice, sugar, and chilli with 2 tbsp of water. Stir until the sugar dissolves. Taste and adjust.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Fill a wide shallow bowl with warm water. Dip a sheet of rice paper for about 10 seconds until just pliable. Lay it flat on a clean, damp surface.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Place 3 halved prawns cut-side down in a line across the lower third of the wrapper. Add a few slices of pork, a small bundle of noodles, some bean sprouts, mint, and coriander.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Fold the sides in, then roll up tightly from the bottom. The prawns should show through the wrapper. Repeat with the remaining wrappers and filling.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Serve the rolls on a plate with the dipping sauce on the side. Scatter with crushed peanuts if you like.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          }
        ],
        "type": "orderedList"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Soak for only 8 to 10 seconds. It will continue to soften as you fill and roll it.",
              "cause": "The wrapper was soaked for too long and became too soft.",
              "symptom": "The rice paper tears when rolling."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Place rolls with a small gap between them. Lay them seam-side down and serve within 30 minutes of making.",
              "cause": "Wet rice paper sticks to itself and other rolls.",
              "symptom": "The rolls stick to each other on the plate."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Use less filling than you think you need. Roll tightly from the bottom and tuck the sides in firmly.",
              "cause": "Too much filling was used or the roll was not tight enough.",
              "symptom": "The filling falls out when biting."
            }
          }
        ],
        "type": "troubleshooter"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Where this dish lives",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Fresh spring rolls are popular throughout southern Vietnam and are especially common in Ho Chi Minh City. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "The name gỏi cuốn means 'salad roll' in Vietnamese. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "They are eaten as a light meal or starter, often at family gatherings. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "Regional variations exist across the country, with some using different herbs or proteins. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "The dish is now widely recognised outside Vietnam as a healthy and fresh alternative to fried spring rolls.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
      }
    ],
    "type": "doc"
  },
  "glossaryTerms": [
    {
      "definition": "Thin, round sheets made from rice flour and water. They are soaked briefly in warm water to become soft and pliable before wrapping.",
      "term": "Rice paper",
      "slug": "rice-paper"
    },
    {
      "definition": "A Vietnamese dipping sauce made from fish sauce, lime juice, sugar, garlic, and chilli. Served alongside many Vietnamese dishes.",
      "term": "Nuoc cham",
      "slug": "nuoc-cham-term"
    }
  ],
